A. weaken $a[0] on the temporary proxy
  STORE[0] ref
  FETCH[0]
  isweak($a[0])=0
  undef $t:
  DESTROY
  FETCH[0]
  defined $a[0]=0 (the proxy's weakening died with the statement)
  STORE[0] undef
B. a held proxy, primed, then weakened: the kill runs the tie's STORE
  STORE[0] ref
  FETCH[0]
  undef $t:
  DESTROY
  STORE[0] undef
  end of B
C. a held proxy reads its cached value; a fresh $a[0] is a new proxy
  STORE[0] ref
  FETCH[0]
  isweak($$r)=1 after a second read (no FETCH: cached)
  FETCH[0]
  isweak($a[0])=0 for a fresh proxy
  undef $t:
  DESTROY
  STORE[0] undef
  end of C
end
